# MANIFEST.md5 -- the fielded static shell 0x72BB0A36 (docs/FIELDED_SHELL.md), the 2026-10 ILA mint.
#
# `md5sum -c MANIFEST.md5` from inside this directory. Generated 2026-09-24 from the mint's build dir,
# which lives in a DETACHED worktree, not in a normal checkout:
#   <repo>/fpga/dfx/build_mint_2026_10/{prod,shell_proj}
# and backed up by stage 8 to <hub-host>:<hub-home>/mints/0x72BB0A36/ (per-static since 987cf26).
#
# static_routed_locked.dcp is the one that matters: every future `make add-rm-*` against this shell
# reads it, and without it no overlay can ever be added to the shell that is on the board.
#
# TWO flashable bases are listed, because the board carried both on 2026-09-24:
#   config_rm_greybox_fw.bit      the mint's own stage-6 bake (firmware c8551081); fielded 08:40
#   config_rm_greybox_fw_v011.bit the same base with firmware v0.11 (987cf264) baked in by updatemem,
#                                 trialled volatile first; ON THE CARD since 09:40 -- THE FIELDED IMAGE
# The ILA RMs' .ltx files are listed with their sidecars and the partial/clearing pair each describes:
# an .ltx travels with its partial (docs/contracts/overlay-manifest.md, "ltx").
#
